ect and scene reconstruction, and SAM 3D Body for human body and shape estimation.\nL178: \nL179: November 19, 2025\nL180: \nL181: cite30†Learn More L182: \nL183: Blog\nL184: \nL185: November 24, 2025\nL186: \nL187: #### Computer Vision\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nChange Log | DeepSeek API Docs (https://api-docs.deepseek.com/updates)\nciteturn31839view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn31835view6\",\"pattern\":\"2025-12-01\"}); Redirected to URL: https://api-docs.deepseek.com/updates/; Total lines: 399\nL131: ## Date: 2025-12-01cite19†​ L132: \nL133: ### DeepSeek-V3.2cite20†​ L134: \nL135: Both `deepseek-chat` and `deepseek-reasoner` have been upgraded to DeepSeek-V3.2.\nL136: \nL137:   * `deepseek-chat` corresponds to DeepSeek-V3.2's non-thinking mode\nL138:   * `deepseek-reasoner` corresponds to DeepSeek-V3.2's thinking mode\nL139: ### DeepSeek-V3.2-Specialecite21†​ L140: \nL141: DeepSeek-V3.2-Speciale is served via a temporary endpoint: base_url=\"cite22†https://api.deepseek.com/v3.2_speciale_expires_on_20251215†api.deepseek.com \". Same pricing as V3.2, no tool calls, available until Dec 15th, 2025, 15:59 (UTC Time).\nL142: \nL143: For more details, please refer to cite23†this documentation .\nL144: \nL145: * * *\nL146: \nL147: ## Date: 2025-09-29cite24†​ L251: ### deepseek-chatcite42†​ L252: \nL253: The deepseek-chat model has been upgraded to DeepSeek-V2.5-1210, with improvements across various capabilities. Relevant benchmarking results include:\nL254: \nL255:   * Mathematical: Performance on the MATH-500 benchmark has improved from 74.8% to 82.8% .\nL256:   * Coding: Accuracy on the LiveCodebench (08.01 - 12.01) benchmark has increased from 29.2% to 34.38% .\nL257:   * Writing and Reasoning: Corresponding improvements have been observed in internal test datasets.\nL341:   * cite2†Date: 2026-09-10 L342:     * cite3†DeepS